<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">păvĕ-făcĭo</span></b> ,
			fēci, factus, 3, v. a.
		paveo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to frighten</i>, <i>alarm</i>, <i>terrify</i> (very rare): pavefacio, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δειλοποιῶ</span>, Gloss. Philox.; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13,
				878</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavefacta pectora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 15, 636</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subito pavefactus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 99</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fumo ac murmure pavefactus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Calig. 51</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ner. 48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2,
				29, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 14,
				20</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavefactus infans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Fur. 1022</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fulgente ejus lumine pavefactus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Psa. 118, 8, §
				17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pavefecit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Qu. in Heptat. 7, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
